WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:09.528
This is Chapter Two, Episode Three: the government, the prime minister, and the courts.

3
00:00:10.078 --> 00:00:14.040
After an election, someone has to actually run the country.

4
00:00:13.991 --> 00:00:18.803
That is the job of the government, the regering, which holds the executive power.

5
00:00:18.803 --> 00:00:22.115
It administers and puts legislation into effect.

6
00:00:22.115 --> 00:00:25.441
But the government also drafts by far the most bills.

7
00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:34.290
In that way, the government normally has the decisive influence on the political agenda, that is, on which current political themes are debated.

8
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:42.153
The government is led by the prime minister, the statsminister, and consists of ministers from one or more parties.

9
00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:49.153
In Danish, a majority government is a flertalsregering, and a minority government is a mindretalsregering.

10
00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:54.403
The parties in the Folketing which together hold government power are called the government parties.

11
00:00:54.403 --> 00:01:00.253
If the government parties together have a majority in the Folketing, we speak of a majority government.

12
00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:09.940
One example of a majority government was the government of 2022 to 26, which consisted of the Social Democrats, Venstre and the Moderates.

13
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:26.460
Other examples were the government of 1978 to 79, which consisted of the Social Democrats and Venstre and was therefore called the SV government, and a government in 1993 to 94 with the Social Democrats and three smaller parties.

14
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:33.873
Since the Second World War, however, the vast majority of governments have been so-called minority governments.

15
00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:46.060
A government is called a minority government if it consists of parties which together do not have such a majority, and therefore need votes from other parties in the Folketing when it needs to build a majority behind its proposals.

16
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.498
The parties outside the government which support a minority government are called support parties.

17
00:01:51.498 --> 00:01:57.966
Members of the Folketing and parties outside the government who are opponents of the government are called the opposition.

18
00:01:58.516 --> 00:02:09.716
Since June 2026, Denmark has had a minority government consisting of the Social Democrats, SF, the Moderates and the Social Liberal Party, the government parties.

19
00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:26.629
The Red-Green Alliance and the Alternative are the government's support parties, while the centre-right parties, Venstre, Liberal Alliance, the Danish People's Party, the Conservative People's Party, the Denmark Democrats and the Citizens' Party, make up the opposition.

20
00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:35.041
On the third of June, 2026, a new government stepped out onto Amalienborg Palace Square after being presented to the king.

21
00:02:35.041 --> 00:02:49.056
In the front row were the party leaders of the four government parties: Lars Løkke Rasmussen of the Moderates, Mette Frederiksen of the Social Democrats, Pia Olsen Dyhr of SF, and Martin Lidegaard of the Social Liberal Party.

22
00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:52.518
Here are the Danish party names you will see on the exam.

23
00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:55.806
Socialdemokratiet, the Social Democrats.

24
00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:56.893
Venstre.

25
00:02:56.893 --> 00:03:00.181
Radikale Venstre, the Social Liberal Party.

26
00:03:00.181 --> 00:03:04.418
Det Konservative Folkeparti, the Conservative People's Party.

27
00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:07.131
SF, Socialistisk Folkeparti.

28
00:03:07.131 --> 00:03:09.268
Moderaterne, the Moderates.

29
00:03:09.268 --> 00:03:10.806
Liberal Alliance.

30
00:03:10.806 --> 00:03:14.094
Dansk Folkeparti, the Danish People's Party.

31
00:03:14.094 --> 00:03:17.168
Enhedslisten, the Red-Green Alliance.

32
00:03:17.168 --> 00:03:19.681
Alternativet, the Alternative.

33
00:03:19.681 --> 00:03:23.231
Danmarksdemokraterne, the Denmark Democrats.

34
00:03:23.231 --> 00:03:26.394
And Borgernes Parti, the Citizens' Party.

35
00:03:26.944 --> 00:03:40.644
The Folketing's four oldest parties, the Social Democrats, Venstre, the Social Liberal Party and the Conservative People's Party, are also the four parties which have been government parties for clearly the most years in total.

36
00:03:40.594 --> 00:03:45.606
That is why these four parties are often referred to as the "government-bearing" parties.

37
00:03:45.606 --> 00:03:55.756
Three parties, the Moderates, the Socialist People's Party and Liberal Alliance, have all been a government party for a shorter period, all under five years.

38
00:03:55.756 --> 00:04:07.140
And five parties, the Denmark Democrats, the Red-Green Alliance, the Alternative, the Danish People's Party and the Citizens' Party, have never been part of a government.

39
00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.552
Now to a key habit of Danish politics.

40
00:04:10.502 --> 00:04:18.802
Since the present election system in its basic structure came about in 1920, no single party has had a majority in the Folketing.

41
00:04:18.802 --> 00:04:24.952
That has created a tradition of the parties trying to agree with each other on how political questions should be solved.

42
00:04:24.952 --> 00:04:33.877
Politicians and parties with very different views and interests often have to talk their way to a compromise that can gather the necessary majority in the Folketing.

43
00:04:33.877 --> 00:04:42.040
And the Folketing passes most laws with a broad majority, which means that the vast majority of its members typically vote in favour.

44
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:49.790
This tradition of broad agreement and cooperation has been called the cooperating democracy, samarbejdende folkestyre.

45
00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.886
It is an important characteristic of the political culture in Denmark.

46
00:04:54.436 --> 00:05:01.873
The politician who, after a general election, has the possibility to form a government is appointed prime minister.

47
00:05:01.823 --> 00:05:05.598
The prime minister is the highest political leader in the country.

48
00:05:05.598 --> 00:05:13.286
It is normally the leader of the largest of the political parties in the government who is appointed prime minister, but it does not have to be so.

49
00:05:13.286 --> 00:05:16.848
A leader of a smaller party can also become prime minister.

50
00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:25.161
For example, Hilmar Baunsgaard of the Social Liberal Party was prime minister from 1968 to 1971.

51
00:05:25.161 --> 00:05:32.023
His party was the smallest party in the government, which also consisted of Venstre and the Conservative People's Party.

52
00:05:32.023 --> 00:05:37.056
What is decisive is that the person does not have a majority against them in the Folketing.

53
00:05:37.606 --> 00:05:40.406
And here are the numbers on who has held the top job.

54
00:05:40.356 --> 00:05:59.206
From the Change of System, Systemskiftet, in 1901 up to 2026, the Social Democrats have held the post of prime minister for a total of 63 years, Venstre for 37 years, the Social Liberal Party for 12 years, and the Conservative People's Party for 10 years.

55
00:05:59.206 --> 00:06:03.930
The other parties in the present Folketing have never held the post of prime minister.

56
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:11.917
The prime minister appoints the other ministers, who get the leadership and the highest responsibility for each their own area.

57
00:06:11.867 --> 00:06:18.142
In principle, it is the individual minister who sets the government's policy in their own area of work.

58
00:06:18.142 --> 00:06:27.924
In practice, it happens in close cooperation with the rest of the government, among other things at government meetings, where the prime minister has the decisive word.

59
00:06:28.474 --> 00:06:33.799
Every minister has a ministry with many civil servants who help the minister in their work.

60
00:06:33.749 --> 00:06:37.461
This applies, for example, when a bill is to be drawn up.

61
00:06:37.461 --> 00:06:42.974
The civil servants in a ministry are employed on the basis of their professional qualifications.

62
00:06:42.974 --> 00:06:48.349
In Denmark there is no tradition of appointing civil servants based on which party they support.

63
00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:50.861
That is for example the case in the USA.

64
00:06:50.861 --> 00:06:56.334
The Danish civil servants are neutral, and they keep their jobs even if a new government comes in.

65
00:06:56.884 --> 00:07:12.096
However, each minister can themselves appoint between one and three so-called special advisers, who are employed in the ministry to give the minister political advice, for example in relation to the Folketing, the rest of the government and the media.

66
00:07:12.046 --> 00:07:22.008
The special advisers are often appointed because they agree with the minister's policy, and unlike the other civil servants, they leave their jobs when a new minister comes in.

67
00:07:22.558 --> 00:07:27.045
The number of ministers is not fixed, but decided by the prime minister.

68
00:07:26.995 --> 00:07:33.133
Since the year 2000, there have been between 17 and 25 ministers in each government.

69
00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:36.808
It can happen that a minister leads several ministries at once.

70
00:07:36.808 --> 00:07:40.508
No formal qualifications are required to become a minister.

71
00:07:40.508 --> 00:07:43.970
Most have, however, great political experience.

72
00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:47.095
A minister does not have to be a member of the Folketing.

73
00:07:47.095 --> 00:08:11.034
Recent examples of ministers appointed without being members of the Folketing are Stephanie Lose of Venstre, who was chair of the regional council in Region of Southern Denmark and was appointed minister for economic affairs in 2023, and Maria Reumert Gjerding of SF, who was president of the Danish Society for Nature Conservation when she became minister for the environment in 2026.

74
00:08:11.584 --> 00:08:17.146
If a minister is not a member of the Folketing, they cannot take part in the Folketing's votes.

75
00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:27.996
A minister does, however, always have access to take part in the Folketing's meetings, and of course must also present bills at the Folketing's podium within their ministerial area.

76
00:08:27.996 --> 00:08:34.164
The Prime Minister's Office is in Prince Jørgen's Courtyard at Christiansborg Palace in Copenhagen.

77
00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:39.314
The Folketing is elected for a period of at most four years at a time.

78
00:08:39.264 --> 00:08:44.051
The prime minister can call a new election at any time during an election period.

79
00:08:44.051 --> 00:08:50.989
This is called the right of dissolution, opløsningsretten, and is the prime minister's weapon against the Folketing.

80
00:08:50.989 --> 00:08:56.790
Because if an election is called, the voters must once more decide who is to be elected.

81
00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:06.665
A new election is often called at a time when there is good support for the government's policy among the voters, and the government thus has good chances of being re-elected.

82
00:09:06.615 --> 00:09:11.965
But it can also happen if the Folketing votes down a government on an important political question.

83
00:09:11.965 --> 00:09:18.940
It is then left to the voters to take a stand on whether they wish to support the government's or the opposition's policy in that area.

84
00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:25.802
After a new election, the prime minister can continue if they still do not have a majority against them in the Folketing.

85
00:09:25.802 --> 00:09:30.384
There is no limit to how many election periods a prime minister may be in power.

86
00:09:30.934 --> 00:09:33.534
Now it is time for your exam practice.

87
00:09:33.484 --> 00:09:38.396
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

88
00:09:38.396 --> 00:09:45.882
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

89
00:09:46.432 --> 00:09:47.682
Question 1.

90
00:09:47.632 --> 00:09:51.819
Can the prime minister appoint a minister who is not a member of the Folketing?

91
00:09:51.819 --> 00:09:53.345
Option A: No.

92
00:09:53.345 --> 00:09:55.092
Option B: Yes.
[DA] Kan statsministeren udpege en minister, der ikke er medlem af Folketinget?  A: Nej  |  B: Ja

93
00:10:01.642 --> 00:10:03.755
The answer is B: Yes.

94
00:10:03.705 --> 00:10:08.334
It appeared in 4 different exams, most recently in May 2024.
[DA] ✔ B: Ja

95
00:10:08.884 --> 00:10:10.134
Question 2.

96
00:10:10.084 --> 00:10:13.809
Can a person be prime minister for more than two election periods?

97
00:10:13.809 --> 00:10:15.434
Option A: Yes.

98
00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:17.088
Option B: No.
[DA] Kan man være statsminister i mere end to valgperioder?  A: Ja  |  B: Nej

99
00:10:23.638 --> 00:10:25.426
The answer is A: Yes.

100
00:10:25.376 --> 00:10:31.338
It appeared in the November 2020, November 2022 and May 2025 exams.
[DA] ✔ A: Ja

101
00:10:31.888 --> 00:10:33.226
Question 3.

102
00:10:33.176 --> 00:10:38.776
Can a government consist of one or more parties that together do not have a majority in the Folketing?

103
00:10:38.776 --> 00:10:40.401
Option A: Yes.

104
00:10:40.401 --> 00:10:42.060
Option B: No.
[DA] Kan en regering bestå af et eller flere partier, der ikke tilsammen har flertal i Folketinget?  A: Ja  |  B: Nej

105
00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:50.398
The answer is A: Yes.

106
00:10:50.348 --> 00:10:56.286
It appeared in the November 2020, November 2021 and November 2025 exams.
[DA] ✔ A: Ja

107
00:10:56.836 --> 00:10:58.136
Question 4.

108
00:10:58.086 --> 00:11:02.699
Which type of government has been most common in Denmark since the Second World War?

109
00:11:02.699 --> 00:11:06.574
Option A: Minority governments, mindretalsregeringer.

110
00:11:06.574 --> 00:11:10.656
Option B: Majority governments, flertalsregeringer.
[DA] Hvilken type regering har været mest almindelig i Danmark siden 2. Verdenskrig?  A: Mindretalsregeringer  |  B: Flertalsregeringer

111
00:11:17.206 --> 00:11:21.306
The answer is A: Minority governments, mindretalsregeringer.

112
00:11:21.256 --> 00:11:25.506
It appeared in the June 2021 and May 2024 exams.
[DA] ✔ A: Mindretalsregeringer

113
00:11:26.056 --> 00:11:27.519
Question 5.

114
00:11:27.469 --> 00:11:33.944
Who can, independently of others, call a general election before the end of the four-year election period?

115
00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:36.919
Option A: The Speaker of the Folketing.

116
00:11:36.919 --> 00:11:39.300
Option B: The prime minister.
[DA] Hvem kan uafhængigt af andre udskrive folketingsvalg inden udløbet af den 4-årige valgperiode?  A: Folketingets formand  |  B: Statsministeren

117
00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.463
The answer is B: The prime minister.

118
00:11:48.413 --> 00:11:52.686
It appeared in the June 2020 and November 2022 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: Statsministeren

119
00:11:53.236 --> 00:11:54.674
Question 6.

120
00:11:54.624 --> 00:12:01.049
Which party has held the post of prime minister for the most years in total since the Change of System in 1901?

121
00:12:01.049 --> 00:12:04.511
The options are Venstre and the Conservative People's Party.

122
00:12:04.511 --> 00:12:06.549
Option A: Venstre.

123
00:12:06.549 --> 00:12:09.624
Option B: The Conservative People's Party.
[DA] Hvilket af følgende partier har haft statsministerposten i sammenlagt flest år siden Systemskiftet i 1901?  A: Venstre  |  B: Det Konservative Folkeparti

124
00:12:16.174 --> 00:12:18.274
The answer is A: Venstre.

125
00:12:18.224 --> 00:12:22.794
It appeared in the November 2022 and June 2026 exams.
[DA] ✔ A: Venstre

126
00:12:23.244 --> 00:12:25.116
Question 7.

127
00:12:25.116 --> 00:12:29.460
Which of the following parties has been in government for the most years in total?

128
00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:33.372
Option A: The Socialist People's Party, SF.

129
00:12:33.372 --> 00:12:37.692
Option B: The Social Liberal Party, Radikale Venstre.

130
00:12:37.692 --> 00:12:40.884
Option C: The Danish People's Party.
[DA] Hvilket af følgende partier har samlet set været i regering flest år?  A: Socialistisk Folkeparti  |  B: Radikale Venstre  |  C: Dansk Folkeparti

131
00:12:47.434 --> 00:12:51.634
The answer is B: The Social Liberal Party, Radikale Venstre.

132
00:12:51.584 --> 00:12:54.462
It appeared in the November 2024 exam.
[DA] ✔ B: Radikale Venstre

133
00:12:55.012 --> 00:12:57.412
That's the end of Part One of Episode 3.

134
00:12:57.362 --> 00:13:01.500
In Part Two, we continue with the courts, domstolene.

135
00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.544
See you there.

